{"tag":"CKLR","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2509.16523","version":"1","local":"theorem-1","file":"","label":"thm-1","number":"1","section":"sec-1","order":1,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm-1}\nGiven an ideal $I=(f_j)_{j\\in J}\\subset K[X_1,X_2,\\dots,X_n]$ such that $\\deg\\, f_j\\leq d$ for all $j\\in J,$ we have $\\mu(I)\\leq\\binom{n+d-1}{d},$ with all generating polynomials chosen to all have degree at most $d.$ This bound is sharp, i.e. equality is achieved, for all choices of $K,n,d.$","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["thm-1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"generating_sets.tex","from":12,"to":14},"hash":"sha256:c0c5f1996a9d77d0bb4caf1b6448cfa40e43a96b8fd0c3bc955fb0813d133468","minhash":"","census":"2509.16523v1#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"M77S","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2509.16523","version":"1","local":"theorem-2","file":"","label":"nullstel-thm","number":"2","section":"sec-1","order":2,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{nullstel-thm}\nEvery minimal generating set $S\\subset K[X_1,\\dots,X_n]$ such that $\\deg f\\leq d$ for all $f\\in S$ satisfies $\\left|S\\right|\\leq\\binom{n+d}{d}.$ This bound is sharp, i.e. equality is achieved, for all $K,n,d$ such that $\\left|K\\right|\u003ed$ (in particular, if $K$ is infinite).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["nullstel-thm"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"generating_sets.tex","from":18,"to":21},"hash":"sha256:2f5d82bd96eff1f1f8ee2b909fcaaa8547f4beaf5405d5dbd94bf51efb8d195b","minhash":"","census":"2509.16523v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"6KP5","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2509.16523","version":"1","local":"proposition-1","file":"","label":"n-equal-1","number":"3","section":"sec-1","order":3,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{n-equal-1}\nAny minimal generating set $S\\subset\\mathbb{F}_q[X]$ such that $\\deg f\\leq d$ for all $f\\in S$ satisfies $\\left|S\\right|\\leq\\lambda_q(d)=\\frac{dq^{O(1)}}{\\log d}.$ Equality is achieved for all $q$ by an explicit construction.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["n-equal-1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"generating_sets.tex","from":22,"to":25},"hash":"sha256:e2e449b6eaf3f187cd095d1c6b579bb8c10e1c15afc24409bd0bc90ef0355807","minhash":"","census":"2509.16523v1#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"V4Q7","kind":"problem","subkind":"conjecture","paper":"2509.16523","version":"1","local":"conjecture-1","file":"","label":"n-greater-1","number":"4","section":"sec-1","order":4,"title":"Conjecture","body_md":"\\label{n-greater-1}\n                                                                                   \n    Every minimal generating set $S\\subset\\mathbb{F}_q[X_1,\\dots,X_n]$ such that $\\deg f\\leq d$ for all $f\\in S$ satisfies $\\left|S\\right|\\leq\\Theta_{n,q}\\left(d/\\log d\\right)^n,$ and equality is achieved for all $n,q.$","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"conjecture","item":"conjecture","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["n-greater-1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"generating_sets.tex","from":27,"to":30},"hash":"sha256:5d8c7fa5567abd7255705a48e504068633973af191df7f7db34b490df9364955","minhash":"","census":"2509.16523v1#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"PJ4V","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2509.16523","version":"1","local":"proposition--1","file":"","number":"3","section":"sec-3","order":5,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"Any minimal generating set $S\\subset\\mathbb{F}_q[X]$ such that $\\deg f\\leq d$ for all $f\\in S$ satisfies $\\left|S\\right|\\leq\\lambda_q(d)=\\frac{dq^{O(1)}}{\\log d}.$ Equality is achieved for all $q$ by an explicit construction.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition*","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","proof_status":"restated","origin":"restated","restates":"proposition-1","span":{"file":"generating_sets.tex","from":77,"to":79},"hash":"sha256:e2e449b6eaf3f187cd095d1c6b579bb8c10e1c15afc24409bd0bc90ef0355807","minhash":"","census":"2509.16523v1#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"9CO2","kind":"problem","subkind":"conjecture","paper":"2509.16523","version":"1","local":"conjecture--1","file":"","number":"4","section":"sec-3","order":6,"title":"Conjecture","body_md":"Every minimal generating set $S\\subset\\mathbb{F}_q[X_1,\\dots,X_n]$ such that $\\deg f\\leq d$ for all $f\\in S$ satisfies $\\left|S\\right|\\leq\\Theta_{n,q}\\left(d/\\log d\\right)^n,$ and equality is achieved for all $n,q.$","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"conjecture*","item":"conjecture","head":"environment","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","proof_status":"restated","origin":"restated","restates":"conjecture-1","span":{"file":"generating_sets.tex","from":116,"to":118},"hash":"sha256:5d8c7fa5567abd7255705a48e504068633973af191df7f7db34b490df9364955","minhash":"","census":"2509.16523v1#env-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"JIJI","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2509.16523","version":"1","local":"proposition-2","file":"","number":"5","section":"sec-4","order":7,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"If $K$ has characteristic $0,$ then an ideal $I\\subset K[X_1,\\dots,X_n]$ with minimal generating set $\\{f_1,\\dots,f_{\\binom{n+d}{d}}\\}$ can be explicitly constructed by considering evaluation points $(d_1,d_2,\\dots,d_n)\\in\\mathbb{N}_0^n$ satisfying $d_1+\\cdots+d_n\\leq d.$","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"generating_sets.tex","from":156,"to":158},"hash":"sha256:93c0300ec6b446a472c06e95d1e856fef71f87d3b93b752bb231e5bfd77ed6f2","minhash":"","census":"2509.16523v1#env-7","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"DLBA","kind":"remark","paper":"2509.16523","version":"1","local":"remark-1","file":"","number":"6","section":"sec-4","order":8,"title":"Remark","body_md":"In general, the $\\binom{n+d}{d}$-many evaluation points form an $n$-dimensional discrete simplex of depth $d+1,$ and the polynomials constructed all have $d$-many linear factors; for each factor, the condition that it is nonzero `peels off' one layer of the simplex.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"remark","item":"remark","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"generating_sets.tex","from":160,"to":162},"hash":"sha256:1b7baf700e68b85d352ecd34d6f95eefbd5e04c12b4950b004d8b452c642da29","minhash":"","census":"2509.16523v1#env-8","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"T8K6","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2509.16523","version":"1","local":"theorem-3","file":"","number":"7","section":"sec-4","order":9,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"For any two nonnegative integers $i,j$ satisfying $i+j\\leq d,$ define $P_{ij}=\\left(\\frac{x^i-y^i}{x^i},\\frac{x^j-y^j}{y^j}\\right)\\in K(x,y)^2.$ If a pair $(x,y)\\in(K^*)^2$ can be chosen such that $x^n\\neq y^n$ for $1\\leq n\\leq d,$ then                                                                                                 \n    an ideal $I\\subset K[X,Y]$ with minimal generating set $\\{f_1,\\dots,f_{\\binom{n+2}{2}}\\}$ can be explicitly constructed by considering evaluation points $P_{ij}.$","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"generating_sets.tex","from":191,"to":194},"hash":"sha256:d9f7ba291e9aed0a3a5199343899c0d726f16bb5f7d1970a89176cac0a3d748e","minhash":"","census":"2509.16523v1#env-9","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
